# EAS Build upload scope. Keep this file IDENTICAL to ../.easignore.
#
# EAS uploads from the git repository root (the folder above), and an
# .easignore replaces every .gitignore. This copy only had client rules, so a
# build swept in server/venv and the admin/website build caches (2.7 GB).
# The rules below are written from the repository root, which is how EAS
# applies them.
#
# The app in client/ is self-contained: nothing outside it is needed to build.

# The rest of the repo (server venv, Next.js build caches, ...)
/server/
/admin/
/website/
/docker-compose.yml
/README.md
/SCREENS.md
.git/

# Reinstalled / regenerated on the build server
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
/client/android/
/client/ios/
/client/dist/
/client/web-build/
**/.kotlin/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.metro-health-check*
**/.vscode/
**/.claude/
**/__pycache__/
**/npm-debug.*
**/yarn-debug.*
**/yarn-error.*
**/.DS_Store

# Docs, not needed to build the app
/client/AGENTS.md
/client/DESIGN.md
/client/README.md

# Secrets: never uploaded. Give the build what it needs as EAS environment
# variables (secret visibility) instead.
**/.env*.local
**/*.pem
**/*firebase-adminsdk*.json
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
**/*.jks
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.mobileprovision
